{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q21098958","formula":"C₂₂H₂₄N₆O₂","hill":"C22H24N6O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":24.0,"N":6.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Emicerfont"},"descriptions":{"en":"Emicerfont (GW-876,008) is a drug developed by GlaxoSmithKline which acts as a CRF-1 antagonist. Corticotropin releasing factor (CRF), also known as Corticotropin releasing hormone, is an endogenous peptide hormone which is released in response to various triggers such as chronic stress, and activates the two corticotropin-releasing hormone receptors: CRF1 and CRF2. This then triggers the release of corticotropin (ACTH), another hormone which is involved in the physiological response to stress."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":11223423,"mass":404.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=C2CCN(C2=N1)C3=C(C=C(C=C3)OC)C)N4C=CC(=N4)N5CCNC5=O","inchikey":"JFHJGXQFESYQGY-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[1-[1-(4-methoxy-2-methylphenyl)-6-methyl-2,3-dihydropyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin-4-yl]pyrazol-3-yl]imidazolidin-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11223423","atoms":54,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":7.405,"y":1.274,"z":-0.026,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.767,"y":2.666,"z":0.101,"el":"O"},{"x":1.896,"y":0.337,"z":0.062,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.507,"y":-1.409,"z":0.046,"el":"N"},{"x":1.626,"y":-2.14,"z":0.033,"el":"N"},{"x":-5.224,"y":0.761,"z":0.055,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.987,"y":-0.147,"z":0.056,"el":"N"},{"x":-6.076,"y":2.871,"z":0.051,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.486,"y":0.846,"z":0.032,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.227,"y":-0.617,"z":0.059,"el":"C"},{"x":0.915,"y":1.409,"z":0.316,"el":"C"},{"x":1.141,"y":-0.882,"z":0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.147,"y":-1.65,"z":0.05,"el":"C"},{"x":3.274,"y":0.572,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.664,"y":-2.952,"z":0.041,"el":"C"},{"x":0.712,"y":-3.142,"z":0.033,"el":"C"},{"x":3.978,"y":0.742,"z